// Basic property: after setting, we can restore using the returned struct.
// We assume (as typical) that the return value represents the previous configuration.
// Even if semantics differ, calling again with 'prev' should still be safe,
// since it's a full function-pointer suite.
valkeyAllocFuncs prev2 = valkeySetAllocators(&prev);
(void)prev2;

// Validation summary: Installed a complete, non-NULL allocator suite and restored prior state to avoid persistent global effects.

// Reset allocators back to library defaults.
